  },
  data: {
    LLM: "1. **Bidding**: Staring left of the dealer, players bid a number of tricks from 6 to 12. Each bid must be higher than the last. 2. **Amerikaner Bid**: The highest possible bid, an commitment to win all 12 tricks without a partner. 3. **The Kitty**: The high bidder takes the 4 kitty cards and discards any 4 cards face down. 4. **Calling the Partner**: The bidder leads the first card. The suit of this card becomes trumps. As they lead, they name a specific card of that suit (e.g., 'The Ace of Spades'). The player holding that card is the secret partner. 5. **Play**: Standard trick-taking rules. Highest card of led suit or highest trump wins the trick.",
    Player: "1. **Bidding**: Staring left of the dealer, players bid a number of tricks from 6 to 12. Each bid must be higher than the last. 2. **Amerikaner Bid**: The highest possible bid, an commitment to win all 12 tricks without a partner. 3. **The Kitty**: The high bidder takes the 4 kitty cards and discards any 4 cards face down. 4. **Calling the Partner**: The bidder leads the first card. The suit of this card becomes trumps. As they lead, they name a specific card of that suit (e.g., 'The Ace of Spades'). The player holding that card is the secret partner. 5. **Play**: Standard trick-taking rules. Highest card of led suit or highest trump wins the trick.",
    objective: 'High bidder must win at least the number of tricks they bid (with their secret partner), or all 12 tricks (if bidding Amerikaner).',
    gameplay: "1. **Bidding**: Staring left of the dealer, players bid a number of tricks from 6 to 12. Each bid must be higher than the last. 2. **Amerikaner Bid**: The highest possible bid, an commitment to win all 12 tricks without a partner. 3. **The Kitty**: The high bidder takes the 4 kitty cards and discards any 4 cards face down. 4. **Calling the Partner**: The bidder leads the first card. The suit of this card becomes trumps. As they lead, they name a specific card of that suit (e.g., 'The Ace of Spades'). The player holding that card is the secret partner. 5. **Play**: Standard trick-taking rules. Highest card of led suit or highest trump wins the trick.",
    keyRules: [
      'Trump Suit: Always the suit of the very first lead made by the bidder.',
      'Grand: An optional bid in some variations where there is no trump suit.',
      'Secret Partner: Must play the called card to the first trick if possible.',
      'Amerikaner Win: If the bidder takes all 12 tricks alone, it is a massive score (+52).',
    ],
